       restart), R4. The missed check: deploy-landed = sha match post-mv, NOT just a new pid — a new
       pid running the OLD binary looks identical to success. REDO LANDED 2026-07-24T07:39Z: [S] rebuilt, verified sha at every hop, /proc/816561/exe=f89abffe (runs the fix, not just on-disk), deploys id=44 now consistent (no more lie). B1 acceptance: broken FROZEN at 682 across ~150 post-deploy events — fix LIVE and holding (primary proof = deterministic code fix; freeze confirmatory; monitor watching overnight). The 682 historical torn lines NOT repaired (repair-vs-annotate = S5 decision). q13 effectively CLOSED pending only the overnight freeze."
    what: "Build+deploy commit 5ba7834 (telemetry_canonical.rs flush_delta cursor fix) to the NUCLEUS.
           STOPS ONGOING CORRUPTION of the canonical Merkle chain. RCA is closed — do NOT re-diagnose."
    rca:  "TOCTOU on the tmpfs size in flush_delta: src_size is sampled by metadata() BEFORE the
           seek+read_to_end. The nucleus keeps appending while we read, so read_to_end consumes past
           src_size; the cursor was then advanced to the STALE src_size, leaving the surplus unmarked,
           and the NEXT flush re-read it and appended it to dst a second time.
           Fix = advance by what was actually read: *bytes_flushed += buf.len()."
    evidence: "681 lines in events.jsonl do not start with '{'. 679 of them are an EXACT SUFFIX of the
           preceding line, duplicated at a uniformly random fraction (0.002-0.998, median 0.508) —
           exactly however much was written during the race. NOT aligned to any power of two (0/681 at
           4096/8192/...) which rules out a buffer flush. No two torn lines adjacent, which rules out a
           split line. Present in every decile, still occurring (35 in the last 20k lines)."
    steps: "1. MANDATORY FIRST: per-file sha256 diff of 108:/root/vsf-nucleus/src against repo HEAD.
               The delta you see is exactly what you will ship. This bit us twice (q4b, q10).
            2. cargo build --release on 108. glibc guard: max symbol must be <= GLIBC_2.36.
            3. R4 deploy to 101 (stop -> CONFIRM pid gone -> mv -> start). Record the deploys row.
            4. Verify: the chain keeps advancing and no NEW suffix-duplicate appears past the deploy
               byte offset. Script: scripts/audit/probe.sh lines <file> gives all counts at once;
               `not-JSON-open` must stop growing. Take the count BEFORE and AFTER."
    warning: "The 681 EXISTING malformed lines are historical damage and are NOT repaired by this fix.
              Do NOT sed/rewrite the canonical chain to clean them — q12 already did that with the
              blank lines and destroyed the diagnostic evidence. Repair-vs-annotate is an S5 decision."
  }

