  q20(S4-OFF-DOMAIN-DECISIONS) priority=P1 owner="[S] measure · [O] adjudicate" {
    ref: "docs/rubric/q19_q17_adjudication_O.vsm §q20_finding"
    found_by: "[O] while adjudicating q19.B — not in any spec issued before now."
    what: "S4's prompt asks an INFRASTRUCTURE question ('System Health Check: RAM {x}GB
           allocated, {y} containers running'). Sampling the last 40 live first_action values,
           the answers are overwhelmingly CLIMATE actions: 'increase sea level mitigation
           efforts', 'improve climate policies', 'change_climate_zones', 'increase ONI',
           'reduce_oni', 'enso', 'marino'. Only a minority are infrastructural."
    why: "num_ctx=256 with num_predict=80 leaves ~176 tokens for a prompt containing a health
           header + 5min of events + a 4-tick dual time series + 5 audit findings + the full
           s1-clima context + the JSON template. llama.cpp truncation keeps the TAIL and drops
           the head — so the clima block and the JSON instruction survive while the 'System
           Health Check' framing is cut. The model answers about the only subject left in its
           window. The code already admits the pressure (line 49: '12 ticks → too large
           prompt'; line 1191: num_ctx lowered 'per L4 tuning' for cycle speed)."
    proportion: "The empty first_action is 1.3%. If this holds, ~98% are answering a different
           question and they PASS the audit, because s4_audit.rs checks only that first_action
           is NON-EMPTY, never that it is RELEVANT. The empty action is not the disease — it is
           the only symptom the current detector has vocabulary for."
    task: "PHASE 1 (measure, do NOT fix): instrument the prompt at the call site in
           s4_operational.rs — log its character and token length for ~10 real cycles alongside
           the resulting first_action. Compare against the ~176-token budget. This is a one-shot
           measurement; it does NOT require waiting for another empty action."
    must_rule_out: "That S4 legitimately carries the clima domain (task S4-MULTI-S1). Rule it out
           honestly. But note the prompt labels that block 'External domain context (s1-clima)' —
           context that should INFORM a decision about the system, not BE the decision."
    ordering: "q20 phase 1 runs BEFORE q19.B's veto. Reason is proportion, not caution: applying
           the veto first hides the 1.3% that is visible and leaves the ~98% untouched and
           unmarked."
    gates_q16: "The S4 dimension of the rescore is BLOCKED on q20. EXP-S4-01 earned its +0.9 in a
           controlled experiment; this is about the live decision path."
  }

